thvor@hotmail.com (Thvor) writes:

> So, anyhow, is there a patch to prevent pets from attacking peaceful
> creatures (shopkeepers, priests, aligned unicorns, etc.)?  This seems
> like a natural thing to want, especially for lawful/neutral
> characters.  As it stands right now, Thvor can't even hit Vinny with a
> rolled up newspaper...
> 
> If someone can point me to such a patch, that'd be great; failing
> that, sections of code that are most likely to need fixing would be
> very appreciated.  I'd also be interested in hearing any reasons why
> pets should be allowed to attack peacefuls, just for completeness. 

I've not heard of such a patch, but I don't imagine it would be too
difficult to write.  There must be something in the code that stops
pets from attacking cockatrices, monsters much more powerful than
them, and so forth - you'd just have to add peacefuls to the list of
monsters that pets won't attack.

I don't think it's very logical for pets to attack everything (that
they have a chance against) either.  For some pets, I suppose it would
be because of their hunting instinct - perhaps your vampire lord is
thirsty for blood and that's why he's killing everyone?  That doesn't
work for non-eating pets, though.  Perhaps your pet's alignment should
make a difference (maybe your vampire lord just likes killing because
he's thoroughly evil?)
Eva.

